# Welcome

 How are you finding the content? Easy? Hard? Just right? We always welcome any feedback from students to help us stay in touch with how you are going and so we can tweak whatever we can to make it more enjoyable for you :) 

**How Do I Improve?**

Please let me know if you have any issues with accessing the videos. I endeavor to load the videos every Thursday morning. These videos are so that you can go over content during the week as it is super normal and expected that you will forget everything! :) No pressure in doing homework but remember the more you listen to the rhythms the easier it will become. Give yourself 6-8 weeks to start hearing and feeling what we do in class. It takes time. Be patient! There is no hurry as long as you are enjoying the process!

**Online Community**

Please join our online community [here.](https://www.facebook.com/groups/559526972928094) I will upload any events or class news and info here. Also, to stay updated in general with Rhythm Culture events such as Camp Afro Foli July 19th-21st. You can follow us [here.](https://www.facebook.com/drumsingdance)

**New Drums Are Coming!**

Expect to see some new drums next week! We are super excited to release these beauties. Bring your cash! If you would like to order a drum which costs no extra, you can choose your colour, sound and size. The drum is then made just for you! We are making drums NOW so it is a great time to put your order in now. **If you buy a drum you get a 4 week course for FREE!**

**Beginners Only Reach Out**

Is there a rhythm or move that you are struggling with? Or is there something you are not sure about? Posture, technique, memory, fundamentals? You can now discuss these with your teacher. Drummers, Nathaniel will be available from 5.15pm on Tuesdays before class to go over anything you are struggling with. Dancers, Bec is available after class from 7.30-7.45pm. Please use this time to touch base and gain tips to improve your experience.
